kosha joint-speed-max

  -- the maximum angular (or linear) speed a joint can sustain
  -- a physical limit imposed by the motor / actuator at that joint
  --
  -- for revolute joints: in radian-per-second
  -- for prismatic joints: in metre-per-second
  --
  -- role in motion planning:
  --   the bottleneck joint — the one where |Δθ| / joint-speed-max is largest —
  --   determines the minimum motion time T for synchronized motion
  --   all other joints are scaled to finish at the same time T
  --   ω[i] = Δθ[i] / T  (actual speed, ≤ joint-speed-max[i])
  --
  -- in the chala-apeksha model:
  --   joint-speed-max is defined in the joint's own frame (chala-apeksha)
  --   the actual world-frame tip velocity depends on the full Jacobian
  --   (joint-speed-max alone does not bound end-effector speed)

  "subanta-swarupa"
  "domain-robotics-sthita kinematic-chain-yukta"
  "angular-velocity-abheda"
  "joint-yukta"
  "radian-per-second-matra"
  "seema-sthita"
  "chala-apeksha-sthita"

shabda joint-speed-max, omega-max, max-speed / the-maximum-angular-speed-of-a-joint-set-by-the-actuator

